213,"outcome":"The Burhanids of Bukhara became vassals in 1207; the Qara Khitai were beaten in the Ilamish Steppe in September 1210; Transoxiana annexed by 1211-12; the Western Kara-Khanids extinguished in 1213.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ala_ad-Din_Muhammad_II"},{"name":"Khwarazmian conquest of Persian Iraq and march on Baghdad","from":1217,"to":1218,"outcome":"By late 1217 all of Persian Iraq was his and Arran, Azerbaijan and Derbent were vassals; the march on Baghdad stopped at the Asadabad Pass in a snowstorm; in February 1218 he removed the caliph's name from the khutba at Merv.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ala_ad-Din_Muhammad_II"},{"name":"Mongol invasion of the Khwarazmian Empire","from":1219,"to":1221,"outcome":"Otrar (September 1219), Bukhara (February 1220), Samarkand (March 1220), Merv (February 1221), Balkh (early 1221), Nishapur (8 April 1221), Parwan (September 1221, a Khwarazmian win) and the Indus (November 1221, a defeat) destroyed the empire.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mongol_conquest_of_Khwarezmia"},{"name":"Jalal ad-Din's wars: Georgia, the Ayyubids and Rum","from":1225,"to":1231,"outcome":"Tbilisi sacked in 1226 (battle of Garni); Akhlat taken 1226 and attacked again 1229; beaten by Kayqubad I at Yassicemen in 1230; Chormagan occupied Northern Iran; Jalal ad-Din killed 15 August 1231.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jalal_ad-Din_Mingburnu"}],"certainty":[{"from":1202,"to":1231,"level":"soft","note":"No survey lines: the Syr Darya, Oxus and Indus frontiers, the vassal rims (Ghur, Arran, Azerbaijan) and the 1221-1231 itinerant state are approximate."}],"sources":[{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Khwarazmian_Empire","title":"Khwarazmian Empire"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ala_ad-Din_Muhammad_II","title":"Ala ad-Din Muhammad II"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mongol_conquest_of_Khwarezmia","title":"Mongol conquest of Khwarezmia"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jalal_ad-Din_Mingburnu","title":"Jalal ad-Din Mingburnu"}]}